#. Tag: title
#: tool-metadataeditor.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Metadata Editor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tool-metadataeditor.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Inside each digital photo hides metadata in the Exif, Iptc, or Xmp formats, "
"and digiKam provides tools for viewing and editing this useful information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tool-metadataeditor.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The application offers metadata editing tools available through the "
"<guimenu>Edit Metadata</guimenu> menu entry. The metadata editor "
"conveniently organizes all metadata into sections for each king of metadata "
"chunck, making it easier to find and edit specific entries. For example, to "
"edit hardware-related information, switch to the Device section. Here you "
"can modify device manufacturer, device model, exposure-related settings, and "
"other information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tool-metadataeditor.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Metadata Editor Working on Device Information from Exif"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tool-metadataeditor.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition to Exif, IPTC and XMP formats are supported, so you can perform "
"the described actions on metadata stored in these metadata chuncks as for "
"Exif. Remember that Exif is dedicated to store camera information, where "
"Iptc and Xmp are more used to store post process text information as rights "
"management. So, it's not recommended to edit the metadata that the camera "
"creates but more to add the author/copyright/etc. information, excepted if "
"you need to fix wrong internal values."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tool-metadataeditor.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Metadata Editor Working on Right Management Information from Xmp"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tool-metadataeditor.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that you can synchronize some specific metadata entries from one chunck "
"to another one, as for example the comments which is available into Exif, "
"Iptc, and Xmpp as different forms. When relevant checkbox are set in the "
"section, relevant chunck entries are backported and adjusted in most "
"compatible format."
msgstr ""
